<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Klement Gottwald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a>–<a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Klement Gottwald was leader of the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> from 1929. He became prime minister after the party's success in the 1946 elections, led the communist seizure of power in February 1948 and succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edvard-benes">Edvard Beneš</a> as president that June. His rule brought Stalinist purges and show trials, and he died in March 1953.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/klement-gottwald.jpg" alt="Klement Gottwald" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R90009,_Budapest,_II._Weltfestspiele,_Festumzug,_tschechische_Delegation_(cropped_KG).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
